{
  "about": "Specification runs through the public build, moved from specification_sources.rs and specification_reports.rs at 5ed2d8a46, whose tests prepared a run (PreparedRun::prepare) and ran it over the input's bytes (execute_csv), or prepared the document alone, and compared the findings the run report renders. A finding of preparation is a refused build of the specification alone, staged with no input; a finding after the input is read is a failed build of the staged input. The negative-zero-division and adam-adlb-ordered-sum specifications and inputs are the benchmarks' own, with the tests' exact-once edits. Compiler findings of a derivation keep their reference paths, context and phase, and an input's unterminated quote is reported before a derivation's grammar; every preflight finding is reported in reference order before any source access; binding collects its ordered findings before dependency findings; an aggregate's grammar findings follow typed ingestion and keep the original path, an unparsed float being reported first; row group declarations and the shared scope keep their authored findings; and a source's condition stays unknown under the normative grammar. No engine output supplied these values.",
